As expected, Ag(QFS)1 frequency spread rapidly in the ‘gene drive’ only cage, reaching maximum frequency at day 70 and rendering the population completely sterile from day 88 leading to population collapse (when no more eggs were produced) (Fig.
4A, C
).

In the ‘gene drive + anti-drive’ cage, the genotype frequency of the Ag(QFS)1 did not exceed 56% (day 14), then progressively declined (as the anti-drive frequency increased), oscillating between 20% and 5% in the last 60 days of the experiment (Fig.
4B
).
